{number: 140}
{title: I Need Thee Every Hour}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] I need Thee every hour,
[Db] Most gracious [Ab] Lord;
No tender voice like Thine
Can [Eb7] peace af-[Ab] ford.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I [Ab] need Thee, O I need Thee;
[Eb7] Every hour I [Ab] need Thee;
O [Db] bless me now, my [Ab] Savior,
I [Eb7] come to [Ab] Thee.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Ab] I need Thee every hour,
[Db] Stay Thou near [Ab] by;
Temptations lose their pow'r
When [Eb7] Thou art [Ab] nigh.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Ab] I need Thee every hour,
In [Db] joy or [Ab] pain;
Come quickly and abide,
Or [Eb7] life is [Ab] vain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Ab] I need Thee every hour,
Teach [Db] me Thy [Ab] will;
And Thy rich promises
In [Eb7] me ful-[Ab] fill.
{end_of_verse}
